# The watcher host's compile list (v0.6.27, P6-DESIGN 1.7): CodexAutoResume.exe, the C# host that loads car_core.dll.
# One repository-relative path per line, in the order csc is given them, under [group] lines, as gui/window.sources is
# written; build/make_gui.ps1 and tests/guiscan.py read it. None of these files is part of the settings window, and the
# window's own list names none of them.
#
#   [host]       the host's Main, the DLL load, the pump and the core's six imports (S6.2b): HostCore.cs, HostMain.cs,
#                HostPump.cs. No ProcessStartInfo, Process.Start or ShellExecute anywhere in this list (P6-DESIGN 1.8)
#   [contract]   gui/ISurfaces.cs: the surfaces' side of the contract (the event and action tables, IHostActions, ISurfaces and
#                the events' classes), which the surfaces post through and implement
#   [standin]    until Integration 10 brings S6.3's [surface] group (car-v0627-s63: the surfaces, gui/SurfaceJson.cs among
#                them, gui/HostSurfaces.cs and gui/SurfaceRender.cs): the JSON class the host reads its replies with, and
#                gui/HostStandIn.cs (SurfaceRender and HostSurfaces that draw nothing). Integration 10 drops this group
#                and HostStandIn.cs, and takes S6.3's [surface] and [generated] groups as they are.

[host]
gui/HostCore.cs
gui/HostMain.cs
gui/HostPump.cs

[contract]
gui/ISurfaces.cs

[standin]
gui/SurfaceJson.cs
gui/HostStandIn.cs
